<title>AUSTRIA: Austrian industry sees Germany, France in EMU.</title>
<headline>Austrian industry sees Germany, France in EMU.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austria's Association of Industry said on Wednesday it expected Germany and France to do everything they could to turn Europe's planned monetary union (EMU) into reality as planned in 1999.</p>
<p>&quot;The euro will happen only with Germany and France, otherwise it won't happen at all,&quot; association president Lorenz Fritz told a news briefing. &quot;We assume that they will do everything to reach this goal.&quot;</p>
<p>Fritz added Austria should prepare itself for a timely start of the single currency and that it could expect to be among the first nations to join.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom, +431 53112 274</p>
